A moved rule that uses a top-level variable of the source file is moved as-is,
with a warning. The assignment itself is never rewritten, only reported.
-- args --
move --src_package=//libc --dst_package=//libc/src/stdlib --include=stdlib_headers
-- in/libc/BUILD.bazel --
STDLIB_HDRS = ["src/stdlib/atoi.h"]

cc_library(
    name = "stdlib_headers",
    hdrs = STDLIB_HDRS,
)
-- out/libc/BUILD.bazel --
STDLIB_HDRS = ["src/stdlib/atoi.h"]
-- out/libc/src/stdlib/BUILD.bazel --
cc_library(
    name = "stdlib_headers",
    hdrs = STDLIB_HDRS,
)
-- stderr --
Moved 1 rules from //libc to //libc/src/stdlib (0 renamed, 0 aliased).
Warnings (2):
  libc/BUILD.bazel:1: [assignment-mentions-moved-file] STDLIB_HDRS mentions "src/stdlib/atoi.h", which moves to //libc/src/stdlib; update it by hand
  libc/BUILD.bazel:3: [dangling-toplevel-var] "stdlib_headers" uses the top-level variable STDLIB_HDRS, which stays in //libc
